1
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:08,140
Excuse me.

2
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:09,780
Coming!

3
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:12,789
Hey, hey, officer,

4
00:00:12,839 --> 00:00:19,120
I want to go to Harajuku. Could you tell
me how to get there? Could you tell me?

5
00:00:20,582 --> 00:00:25,640
then take the train, change to the Sobu Line at Akihabara,
and it's the second stop.

6
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:28,660
Thanks a lot, officer.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,980
Well then, I'm not going to Harajuku.

8
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:33,420
It's fine.

9
00:00:33,420 --> 00:00:36,000
Harajuku for the fat is Ryogoku.

10
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,580
It's Sanpei.

11
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:44,540
When you watch TV,

12
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:47,160
turn the room lights on and watch from a distance,
would you?

13
00:00:55,960 --> 00:01:00,280
Anyone who's broke, come see me.

14
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:04,980
I'm broke too, but don't worry.

15
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:08,840
Look at the blue sky,

16
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:12,080
white clouds.

17
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:12,420
Well,

18
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:16,520
somehow or other,

19
00:01:16,520 --> 00:01:18,860
it'll work out, right?

20
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:20,820
Somehow or other,

21
00:01:20,820 --> 00:01:22,500
Hahahaha.

22
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:23,500
Hahahaha.

23
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:24,000
Hahahaha.

24
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,680
Hahahaha.

25
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:26,180
Hahahaha.

26
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:34,380
Anyone without a job,

27
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:36,000
come see me.

28
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,450
I don't have one either,

29
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:40,450
but don't worry.

30
00:02:21,980 --> 00:02:26,620
That's it.

31
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:47,040
You piece-of-junk stove!

32
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:47,500
Damn it!

33
00:02:48,820 --> 00:02:49,380
Whoa!

34
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:52,880
This is unbearable!

35
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:54,720
My hands are numb from the cold,

36
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:55,780
I can't get it working right.

37
00:02:57,480 --> 00:02:58,280
Hot!

38
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:00,280
Damn it!

39
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:03,340
Somehow,
nature is making me angrier and angrier.

40
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:04,940
Why is it only me

41
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:06,620
who has to go through this?

42
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:09,760
It's Nakagawa and Reiko's
fault in the first place!

43
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:11,300
What did you say?

44
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:17,640
Well, suddenly I have to attend a party

45
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:20,520
hosted by my father for the business elite,
standing in for him.

46
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:26,240
If I don't go, it could affect
the future of the Japanese economy.

47
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:27,002
Well,

48
00:03:27,052 --> 00:03:30,660
I've been taken care of by the Nakagawa Konzern before,
after all.

49
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:32,760
Fine, I'll take your place.

50
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:35,700
Thank you, senpai, I'm in your debt.

51
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:36,820
In return,

52
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:40,320
I understand,
I'll make it up to you someday.

53
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:43,160
If it's going to be anything,
how about fugu?

54
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:46,620
Fugu sashimi, fried fugu,
fugu chili, and fugu zosui.

55
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:48,380
Senpai, the time...

56
00:03:48,380 --> 00:03:50,700
Right, and of course, hot fin sake too.

57
00:03:51,260 --> 00:03:54,160
Yeah, yeah, well, sorry,
I'll leave the rest to you.

58
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:57,220
Leave it to me, yeah, yeah.

59
00:03:57,220 --> 00:04:00,040
Well, now that's settled, the night is long.

60
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:04,260
Since I've got nothing better to do, I might
as well spend the whole night finishing this.

61
00:04:04,260 --> 00:04:05,820
Ryo-chan, I'm heading out first.

62
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:09,740
Reiko, you're leaving?
It's not time yet, you know.

63
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:15,160
But I told you I'd leave early today because I
have a drinking party with Komachi and the others.

64
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:17,080
Was that right?

65
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:23,200
Honestly, Ryo-chan, I brought you a cake the other
day as a advance payment for that favor, remember?

66
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:27,060
Yeah, I guess so.

67
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:30,280
Ryo-chan, you forget things as soon
as you've taken a couple of steps.

68
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:32,620
Don't treat me like a chicken.

69
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:34,940
But a promise is a promise.

70
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:39,500
Yeah, yeah, fine.
Just hurry up and get going, won't you.

71
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:44,880
I'm going, then. Bye, Ryo-chan.
What do you mean, "bye"?

72
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:58,260
I'm out here shivering from the cold, and those bastards are in a warm room, stuffing their faces with good booze and good food on the company's dime.
And worst of all is the Chief.

73
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:05,500
Is anyone here?
Oi, it's trouble, it's the Chief!

74
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:07,540
Yes, I'm coming right now.

75
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:10,600
Chief, is something wrong?

76
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:14,280
I heard from Nakagawa that
you took over his night shift.

77
00:05:14,280 --> 00:05:18,340
Yes, I did it for a cute junior,
and for Japan's economy.

78
00:05:18,340 --> 00:05:20,740
It was absolutely not for the fugu.

79
00:05:20,740 --> 00:05:25,080
Don't tell me you asked Nakagawa for something again,
for fugu.

80
00:05:26,140 --> 00:05:30,100
It's just the big heart of a senpai like me,
that's all.

81
00:05:31,700 --> 00:05:35,320
Well, never mind. Ryotsu, something
urgent has come up for a business trip.

82
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:38,480
You have to take the 9 o'clock bullet train.

83
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:42,320
I have to go home and get ready right away.

84
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:44,060
Sorry, but I'm leaving the rest to you.

85
00:05:44,060 --> 00:05:50,020
Yes! Ryotsu Kankichi will hold down this
station admirably while the Chief is away.

86
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:54,040
Don't go making grand speeches.
Just do your job properly.

87
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:54,880
See you.

88
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:56,360
Have a good trip.

89
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:01,340
Now I can stretch my
legs without holding back.

90
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:08,000
And whatever you do, don't go handicapping horse races
with the red pencil behind your ear during work hours.

91
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:09,720
I'm counting on you.

92
00:06:12,260 --> 00:06:14,180
Why is it only me?

93
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:17,040
It's so pathetic it makes me cry.

94
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:25,100
Damn it, Terai's just as bad!

95
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:31,360
Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box.

96
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,440
Ryo-san?

97
00:06:33,780 --> 00:06:35,600
What is it? What's Terai done now?

98
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:39,520
He's come down with a cold
and has a 39-degree fever!

99
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:42,540
39 degrees is his normal temperature,
isn't it?

100
00:06:42,540 --> 00:06:45,080
I'm not like you, Ryo-san.

101
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:49,740
At 39 degrees, my head's spinning
and my nose won't stop running!

102
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:52,940
I'm coughing nonstop, I'm practically dying!

103
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:55,780
Damn it, so what's your point?

104
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:59,760
So I'm sorry,
but please let me take the day off!

105
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:04,000
Idiot, stop! You'll give me your cold!

106
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,640
Can you catch it over the phone?

107
00:07:07,520 --> 00:07:09,840
Fine, fine. Just go to bed.

108
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:12,660
Ryo-san, you really are kind after all.

109
00:07:16,900 --> 00:07:18,620
Damn it, I can't take this anymore!

110
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:21,580
Wind, cold, whatever.
Here it's just a draft through the gaps.

111
00:07:21,580 --> 00:07:23,060
Is everyone like this?

112
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:31,740
No way.

113
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:36,200
I went and made the floor eat
the last cup noodles I had left.

114
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:43,000
Shit, this is the worst.

115
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,740
Why do I always have to go through this?

116
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:48,740
Nakagawa's, Reiko's, and Terai's shares too.

117
00:07:48,740 --> 00:07:51,940
I'm the one working, and what is this?

118
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:54,280
Damn it, I can't take this anymore.

119
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:56,280
If I keep going like this,
I'll get lost out in the cold

120
00:07:58,360 --> 00:07:59,380
and get found in a state of collapse.

121
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:08,880
Excuse me for a moment.

122
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:10,660
Hello?

123
00:08:11,820 --> 00:08:13,180
Is this you, senior?

124
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:15,420
Nakagawa, this is bad!

125
00:08:15,420 --> 00:08:16,820
Th-this is bad, you say?

126
00:08:16,820 --> 00:08:18,060
What's the incident?

127
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:19,740
Is there meat there?

128
00:08:19,740 --> 00:08:22,680
Meat? Yes, there is.

129
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:23,820
Why? What about it?

130
00:08:23,820 --> 00:08:26,020
Nobody's eaten it yet, have they?

131
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:26,720
No.

132
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:29,160
Thank goodness, I made it in time!

133
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:33,120
Made it in time? Senior,
is there something wrong with the meat?

134
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:35,740
I can't say that right now.

135
00:08:35,740 --> 00:08:39,820
Listen, Nakagawa, bring that
meat to the police box right away!

136
00:08:39,820 --> 00:08:42,760
Senpai, what do you mean, the police box?

137
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:45,120
Don't raise your voice!

138
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:45,640
Yes.

139
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:49,000
We just got a top-secret
message from headquarters.

140
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:49,840
Yes.

141
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:51,780
Listen, it has to be the raw kind!

142
00:08:51,780 --> 00:08:54,780
And don't forget the
ponzu and other seasonings!

143
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:55,600
Seasonings?

144
00:08:56,020 --> 00:09:01,580
Seasonings! You don't know what's in the seasonings either,
not just the meat, so hurry!

145
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:02,840
Understood.

146
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:09,860
Yay!

147
00:09:09,860 --> 00:09:12,280
When it's cold,
hotpot is the best, isn't it?

148
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,920
I wonder who that is.

149
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:17,060
Reiko, it's from your boyfriend!

150
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:21,200
Ugh, I don't have any such person. Hello?

151
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:23,620
It's you, Reiko. It's a disaster!

152
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:26,920
Ryo-chan? What? What happened?
What do you mean, disaster?

153
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:29,360
It's the Chief, the Chief...

154
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,880
What? What's wrong with the Chief?

155
00:09:33,060 --> 00:09:34,220
The Chief...

156
00:09:35,660 --> 00:09:38,980
I can't understand you if you're just crying.
Pull yourself together, Ryo-chan.

157
00:09:38,980 --> 00:09:42,980
The Chief's life is hanging by a thread.

158
00:09:42,980 --> 00:09:44,220
What?

159
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:47,925
According to the doctor,
he's overworked his nerves,

160
00:09:47,975 --> 00:09:50,500
and he only has a few days left.

161
00:09:51,100 --> 00:09:51,500
No way!

162
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:55,380
Apparently it's from a lack
of vitamins and calcium.

163
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:57,700
If we get him to eat vegetables,
he might pull through.

164
00:09:58,340 --> 00:10:01,420
Come quickly, Reiko, before it's too late!

165
00:10:01,420 --> 00:10:03,600
Got it, I'll come right away.

166
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:06,060
Thanks. And don't forget the vegetables.

167
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:08,780
Chinese cabbage, garland chrysanthemum,
long green onions, and things like that.

168
00:10:08,780 --> 00:10:13,080
Also, shirataki noodles and
seafood are supposedly good too.

169
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,700
Fugu especially.

170
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:17,280
Bring it to the police box right away.

171
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:20,220
Please, Reiko, it's for the Chief!

172
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:25,600
Yes, this is Terai.

173
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:27,320
Ryo-san, what is it?

174
00:10:27,500 --> 00:10:29,380
Way to go, Terai, congratulations.

175
00:10:29,380 --> 00:10:31,600
Congratulations? I've got a cold, you know.

176
00:10:32,380 --> 00:10:35,880
Hey, brace yourself,
about that clay pot you have at home.

177
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:36,860
Clay pot?

178
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:40,240
Yeah, remember when we had
hotpot at your place once?

179
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,700
Yeah.

180
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:42,735
The Chief, you see,

181
00:10:42,785 --> 00:10:46,880
brought in someone who'd pay
a million yen for that clay pot.

182
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:48,180
A million yen?

183
00:10:49,540 --> 00:10:50,260
A million?

184
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:52,960
Bring it to the departure gate!

185
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:57,160
But that one, I bought it at
the supermarket for 2,980 yen.

186
00:10:58,300 --> 00:10:59,240
Something like that.

187
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:01,640
Anyone who knows what to look
for can tell the difference.

188
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:04,060
By mistake,
a Living National Treasure's work

189
00:11:04,060 --> 00:11:06,680
ended up mixed in with the bargain goods.

190
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:10,320
B-but in this condition...

191
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:12,140
We have to leave right now.

192
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:14,560
The buyer is a foreigner, you know.

193
00:11:14,560 --> 00:11:15,640
A foreigner?

194
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:16,760
No, wait a minute.

195
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:18,520
I'll go get him right now.

196
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:20,324
That's done, and now I'm busy.

197
00:11:20,374 --> 00:11:22,800
If we don't hurry, the plane will leave.

198
00:11:22,940 --> 00:11:25,960
Please, somehow.
We don't have any time left.

199
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:30,180
Can you come or not, Terai?
The million's going to slip away!

200
00:11:30,740 --> 00:11:33,540
I-I'm coming, right now.
Keep that person waiting.

201
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:42,260
Oops. I forgot to turn off the power. Yes.

202
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:43,160
Ba, ba, Barba.

203
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:44,838
It's Ryotsu.

204
00:11:44,888 --> 00:11:47,900
I'm right in the middle of a survival game.
I'm hanging up.

205
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:49,840
Help me, Bolbo!

206
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:52,460
What's wrong? Ryotsu! Ryotsu!

207
00:11:56,300 --> 00:11:57,980
Bobby, I win.

208
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:00,880
Jodie.

209
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:03,400
Bolbo! Are you listening? Bolbo!

210
00:12:03,760 --> 00:12:06,660
Bring the portable gas
stove over right away!

211
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:08,920
Without a portable gas stove...

212
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:11,660
Whoa! Whoa! Stop!
Bring the gas stove, quick!

213
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:14,680
I don't get it, but Ryotsu's in trouble!

214
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:20,880
Hello?

215
00:12:21,420 --> 00:12:23,320
What? Is that you, Ryo-san?

216
00:12:23,820 --> 00:12:25,040
What did you say?!

217
00:12:26,140 --> 00:12:27,900
Hehehe, how about it?

218
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,780
With this,
we can have a lavish hot pot party!

219
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:33,180
Ahahahaha!

220
00:12:33,180 --> 00:12:35,640
Ahahahaha!

221
00:12:48,820 --> 00:12:51,020
Senpai, I brought the meat.

222
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:56,280
Senpai?

223
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:00,880
Ryo-chan.

224
00:13:00,880 --> 00:13:03,260
Ryo-san, I brought the pot.

225
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:04,620
Ryotsu, are you all right?

226
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:07,360
Senpai,
I brought the ingredients for egg sake.

227
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:09,600
But isn't this a bit much?

228
00:13:11,140 --> 00:13:14,460
You made it. Thanks, everyone, thanks.

229
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:16,780
Senpai, what exactly is going on?

230
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:21,280
With all this seafood,
it's like we're having a hot pot party.

231
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:23,460
Ding-ding! Exactly right.

232
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:29,120
Well, I had you all gather
for an emergency drill, but

233
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:32,940
it's freezing, so I figured we
might as well have a hot pot.

234
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:35,480
An emergency drill? Don't make me laugh.

235
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,140
You've got to be kidding me!

236
00:13:37,140 --> 00:13:38,400
Yeah, Ryo-san!

237
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:40,860
What about the million yen?

238
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:44,560
Don't get so worked up.
Hot pot is meant to be enjoyed.

239
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:47,240
Enjoy it? After tricking people like that?

240
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:54,860
I'm here with a 39-degree fever!
This is too much, Ryo-san. It's just cruel.

241
00:13:55,280 --> 00:13:59,500
Ryo-saaan! Okay, I'm sorry, I was wrong.

242
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:05,660
I, I'm not going to be
fooled by your act. I see.

243
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:12,400
How sad. To be spoken to like that by comrades
I've shared so many years of ups and downs with.

244
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,320
So it's goodbye to this locker, too.

245
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:18,600
I'll miss this desk too,

246
00:14:18,600 --> 00:14:21,240
Did something happen, senior?

247
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:24,700
I got beaten by the Chief over
this logbook so many times.

248
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:27,560
Ryo-chan, what's wrong with you?

249
00:14:27,560 --> 00:14:29,980
This night shift, packed with memories,

250
00:14:29,980 --> 00:14:31,460
Hey, Ryotsu.

251
00:14:31,460 --> 00:14:32,820
Ryo-san.

252
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:34,400
Senior.

253
00:14:36,060 --> 00:14:37,580
No, it's nothing.

254
00:14:37,580 --> 00:14:39,800
This is my problem alone.

255
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:41,220
What happened?

256
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:48,860
Well, I'd like to talk about
this slowly over some hot pot.

257
00:14:49,940 --> 00:14:52,920
Did you screw up again and have
to write another letter of apology?

258
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:56,540
But the senior wouldn't be this
down over something so minor.

259
00:14:56,540 --> 00:14:58,040
Then could it be...

260
00:14:58,540 --> 00:14:59,900
Dismissal from service.

261
00:15:02,100 --> 00:15:03,420
So you're getting fired?

262
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:05,800
Is that right, Ryo-chan?

263
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:08,900
Don't make me say it outright.

264
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:09,380
But...

265
00:15:09,380 --> 00:15:09,620
But...

266
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:13,080
Life's a lot like hot pot, isn't it.

267
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:14,860
What's that supposed to mean?

268
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:15,960
I don't get it.

269
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:18,900
Tell us the truth. Are you fired?

270
00:15:19,040 --> 00:15:20,100
Senior...

271
00:15:21,260 --> 00:15:23,160
Come on, what do you say?

272
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:24,940
Let's just have a hot pot instead.

273
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:27,080
It's our last supper.

274
00:15:27,580 --> 00:15:28,920
Last supper?

275
00:15:29,180 --> 00:15:31,620
So you're really getting fired?

276
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:33,360
Uuugh...

277
00:15:33,940 --> 00:15:35,320
Y-yeah, I guess so.

278
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:37,160
Here, we should do as
the senior officer says,

279
00:15:37,160 --> 00:15:38,760
and have some hot pot.

280
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:39,960
That's right.

281
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:43,060
Since we've got the ingredients and the pot all ready,
after all.

282
00:15:43,060 --> 00:15:45,580
We've got a portable gas stove too!

283
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:46,500
Yes!

284
00:15:46,500 --> 00:15:47,860
And there's sake, too.

285
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:49,300
Thanks, everyone.

286
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:51,920
Your kindness really touches me.

287
00:16:00,060 --> 00:16:02,320
Excuse me,
do you know where the president is?

288
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:05,480
Someone called him, you know.

289
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:07,560
Something about meat, he said.

290
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:09,700
He left with a changed look on his face.

291
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:10,320
Meat.

292
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:13,480
That was no ordinary look.

293
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:16,100
It seems there's some kind of secret.

294
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:16,940
Secret.

295
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:20,360
Don't tell me the meat
our company is developing

296
00:16:23,060 --> 00:16:24,120
Yeah, it's me.

297
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:25,760
What?

298
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:28,740
The top-secret microchip meat in development

299
00:16:29,760 --> 00:16:31,140
Got it. I'll look into it.

300
00:16:38,420 --> 00:16:39,920
T-this is terrible!

301
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:41,740
Nick's file is missing!

302
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:44,060
This is an international conspiracy!

303
00:16:46,020 --> 00:16:46,860
Colonel Bakuryu!

304
00:16:46,860 --> 00:16:47,480
Yes?

305
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:50,860
Colonel, there was a message
from the young lady just now.

306
00:16:50,860 --> 00:16:52,700
From Jodie?

307
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:54,980
She said she's bringing the gas stove

308
00:16:54,980 --> 00:16:56,480
and that we don't need to come pick her up.

309
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:58,660
What? The gas stove?

310
00:16:59,680 --> 00:17:00,220
Exactly how did she put it?!

311
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:03,090
The code name "Gashi-kun" means

312
00:17:03,140 --> 00:17:05,160
the code name for emergency alert status!

313
00:17:16,820 --> 00:17:17,540
I'm sorry.

314
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:21,980
An important report has come
in from the Staff Colonel.

315
00:17:21,980 --> 00:17:22,460
Mm.

316
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:27,380
A terrorist with a new weapon in Kameari,
Katsushika, Japan...?

317
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:30,320
What? Report to the president immediately!

318
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:36,260
Reiko-san rushed out with a terrified
look on her face and hasn't come back.

319
00:17:36,260 --> 00:17:39,160
Something must have happened at the Kameari Kōen-mae police box,
I'm sure of it.

320
00:17:40,060 --> 00:17:43,720
Maybe it's an alien invasion
or something like that.

321
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:45,040
Excellent.

322
00:17:48,060 --> 00:17:49,800
It's noisy. Did something happen?

323
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:54,240
They say the whole Kameari area has
been completely invaded by aliens.

324
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:55,320
Seriously?

325
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:57,520
Apparently Chinese cabbage
and tofu are effective.

326
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:03,380
What? From the U.S. Department of Defense?

327
00:18:03,780 --> 00:18:08,460
Just now, I also got a call from the business
community saying there's an international conspiracy.

328
00:18:09,780 --> 00:18:11,160
President, it's an emergency!

329
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:12,780
What's going on?

330
00:18:12,780 --> 00:18:16,100
It seems something abnormal has happened
at the Kameari Kōen-mae police box.

331
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:19,100
I understand. Bring Ohara back immediately.

332
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:26,880
What? The Kameari Kōen-mae police
box will head there right away.

333
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:27,980
This is bad.

334
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:32,260
Well, it should be about time now.

335
00:18:32,260 --> 00:18:35,480
Come on, Ryo-chan,
you can tell us now, can't you?

336
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:36,540
That's...

337
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:39,760
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

338
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:43,460
Leave this to the hot pot master.

339
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:44,600
Wonderful!

340
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:45,920
How rude!

341
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:46,480
Aaaaaah!

342
00:18:48,860 --> 00:18:56,660
First we'll rescue the bad guy, then we'll add the meat later so it doesn't get too tough.
Somehow that face just doesn't look right, does it?

343
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:11,020
This is serious! I'm Ohara, the person in charge of this police box.
An alien invasion from a UFO?

344
00:19:11,020 --> 00:19:18,140
Is that true?! Some idiot international terrorist came to
the police box with a new murder device and attacked it!

345
00:19:18,140 --> 00:19:27,720
Terrorist, why is a terrorist attacking the police box?
Are the attack preparations ready? A ferocious carnivorous monster? No, it's a terrorist!

346
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:29,380
Isn't it aliens?

347
00:19:29,380 --> 00:19:31,240
It's a carnivorous monster!

348
00:19:31,360 --> 00:19:32,260
It's a terrorist!

349
00:19:32,420 --> 00:19:33,260
It's aliens!

350
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:34,460
It's a terrorist!

351
00:19:34,540 --> 00:19:35,240
It's aliens!

352
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:36,100
Terrorist!

353
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:36,880
Aliens!

354
00:19:36,900 --> 00:19:37,440
Terrorist!

355
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,720
Anyway, attack!

356
00:19:40,340 --> 00:19:41,400
W-wait, please!

357
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:43,960
My subordinate is being held hostage.

358
00:19:43,960 --> 00:19:49,440
I hear the criminal's demand is 2,980 yen,
isn't that right?

359
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:55,360
Chief, Colonel Bakuryu
is trying to reach you.

360
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:56,020
What?

361
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:01,060
We'll reach the target in five minutes.

362
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:04,400
If you give the go-ahead,
we can fire the missiles at any time.

363
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:05,860
No, that's not allowed.

364
00:20:05,860 --> 00:20:07,960
My subordinate, Ryotsu, is in there.

365
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:08,820
You can't do that.

366
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:10,740
It looks like there are seven people inside.

367
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:12,440
There's a heat source in the center.

368
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:14,080
Could that be the new weapon?

369
00:20:16,040 --> 00:20:17,560
We can't just stand by and do nothing.

370
00:20:23,780 --> 00:20:24,140
What?

371
00:20:27,380 --> 00:20:30,140
Leave this to us, MIB.

372
00:20:30,140 --> 00:20:31,280
What are you talking about?

373
00:20:31,280 --> 00:20:34,840
Protecting Japan's peace is our job.

374
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:35,700
No.

375
00:20:36,140 --> 00:20:39,060
We protect the peace of the Earth.

376
00:20:40,720 --> 00:20:42,560
Life is hot pot, hot pot!

377
00:20:42,560 --> 00:20:45,120
By the way, Ryo-san, what really happened?

378
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:50,240
Take your time, Ryo-chan.

379
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:51,800
The night is long, after all.

380
00:20:51,800 --> 00:20:52,920
That's right.

381
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:55,000
Alright, you can start with the vegetables.

382
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:58,180
He reached for the bomb.

383
00:20:59,120 --> 00:21:01,000
Right, SWAT team, get into position.

384
00:21:02,080 --> 00:21:04,720
If anything happens to Ryotsu by any chance,
because of this...

385
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:08,680
Yes, by phone. We'll ask the
culprit's demands over the phone.

386
00:21:12,220 --> 00:21:14,560
Alright,
the meat should be ready to eat about now.

387
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:17,700
Who is it?
We were just getting to the good part.

388
00:21:17,700 --> 00:21:19,260
Yes, yes, what happened?

389
00:21:19,260 --> 00:21:20,820
Ryotsu, are you all right?

390
00:21:20,820 --> 00:21:22,280
Chief!

391
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:24,480
Oh no.

392
00:21:26,380 --> 00:21:27,660
Calling on the phone is dangerous.

393
00:21:27,660 --> 00:21:30,280
If we provoke the culprit,
there's no telling what he'll do.

394
00:21:31,300 --> 00:21:33,280
The SWAT team is in position.

395
00:21:34,020 --> 00:21:35,720
Alright, everyone, wait for orders.

396
00:21:36,260 --> 00:21:38,080
One minute until we reach the target.

397
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:41,040
All units, get into attack formation.

398
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:44,320
Isn't it kind of noisy outside?

399
00:21:45,180 --> 00:21:46,420
Terai!

400
00:21:46,420 --> 00:21:47,880
Terai, shut it!

401
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:52,460
Terai was being held hostage too?

402
00:21:52,460 --> 00:21:55,380
Could Nakagawa and Reiko be hostages too?

403
00:21:56,160 --> 00:21:58,340
Please pull the SWAT team back.

404
00:21:58,780 --> 00:22:01,660
There's a risk my subordinates will
be shot by mistake for the culprits.

405
00:22:01,660 --> 00:22:02,680
I'm counting on you.

406
00:22:03,820 --> 00:22:06,000
Alright, let's switch to the storming plan.

407
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:08,820
B2 unit, ready to attack.

408
00:22:08,820 --> 00:22:10,760
C3 unit, ready to attack.

409
00:22:10,760 --> 00:22:12,680
D4 unit, ready to attack.

410
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:14,200
Alright, let's go!

411
00:22:18,860 --> 00:22:21,380
Alright, now the moment we've been waiting for.
The sacred meat!

412
00:22:21,380 --> 00:22:22,820
Let's eat!

413
00:22:24,500 --> 00:22:25,480
That voice...

414
00:22:26,780 --> 00:22:28,160
Excuse me, excuse me.

415
00:22:28,280 --> 00:22:30,640
Then I'll eat the meat.

416
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:34,000
Oh no, what should I do?

417
00:22:41,960 --> 00:22:42,780
What is it?

418
00:22:43,180 --> 00:22:45,960
That vicious face... he's the culprit!

419
00:22:46,140 --> 00:22:47,020
Catch him!

420
00:22:47,820 --> 00:22:48,560
What's going on?

421
00:22:49,840 --> 00:22:50,700
Stop!

422
00:22:50,900 --> 00:22:52,560
Stop!

423
00:23:02,720 --> 00:23:05,320
Target located, capturing.

424
00:23:09,100 --> 00:23:10,000
Capture complete.

425
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:12,640
We have the alien in custody.

426
00:23:20,300 --> 00:23:21,380
What is that?

427
00:23:22,560 --> 00:23:25,400
The hostages have been safely rescued.
Please return to base.

428
00:23:25,400 --> 00:23:26,220
Roger.

429
00:23:29,020 --> 00:23:32,320
Thank goodness, everyone's safe.

430
00:23:32,840 --> 00:23:33,800
Where's Ryotsu?

431
00:23:48,860 --> 00:23:51,060
What on earth is going on?

432
00:23:52,560 --> 00:23:53,040
Let me save them!

433
00:23:53,360 --> 00:23:54,680
What a lively alien.

434
00:23:54,680 --> 00:23:56,860
Hey, wait! What are you doing?!

435
00:23:57,660 --> 00:24:00,420
Stop! I'm not an alien!

436
00:24:00,940 --> 00:24:02,080
Help me!

437
00:24:22,560 --> 00:24:27,360
I don't think I want to be
the kind who fights to win,

438
00:24:27,360 --> 00:24:31,960
if you're just rotting
at the bend in the road,

439
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:34,300
the moon has run away.

440
00:24:34,300 --> 00:24:38,040
Because now isn't everything,

441
00:24:38,040 --> 00:24:42,540
don't take it too seriously.

442
00:24:42,540 --> 00:24:46,260
Even if you fudge things a little,

443
00:24:46,260 --> 00:24:50,420
once in a while, you help someone.

444
00:24:50,420 --> 00:24:54,013
Baby, do you know me?

445
00:24:54,063 --> 00:24:56,840
Facing tomorrow, with a nice spirit,

446
00:24:57,860 --> 00:25:04,260
we won't rot; we'll do what needs doing,
with a cute spirit.

447
00:25:04,260 --> 00:25:11,460
It's hard to understand
because I want to look that way.

448
00:25:12,480 --> 00:25:17,340
Better than all show
and no substance, right?

449
00:25:30,160 --> 00:25:31,820
Delivery Police!

450
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:34,840
A convenience store nearby
beats a police box far away.

451
00:25:34,840 --> 00:25:37,240
If there's a police box right inside
the convenience store down the street,

452
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:39,320
the neighborhood's crime
prevention goes up too.

453
00:25:39,320 --> 00:25:43,720
This is the Columbus's egg of ideas:
a brilliant two-birds-one-stone plan!

454
00:25:44,240 --> 00:25:46,980
Next time, the police box dispatches
from the convenience store!

455
00:25:47,340 --> 00:25:47,960
Take care!

